<title>BELGIUM: SNC-Lavalin has $33 mln Belgian loan for gas plant.</title>
<headline>SNC-Lavalin has $33 mln Belgian loan for gas plant.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said on Friday it would give a $33.6 million, 10-year export credit loan with a fixed 6.64 percent interest rate to  SNC-Lavalin Europe for work it is doing at the Rhourde Nouss gas complex in Algeria.</p>
<p>SNC-Lavalin Europe, a Belgian subsidiary of Canada's SNC-Lavalin International, is a sub-contractor on the project, which is led by Algerian state oil and gas firm Sonatrach, the government said in a statement after its weekly cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>The expansion of the Rhourde Nouss gas complex will help ensure gas deliveries to Europe through the so-called Maghreb gas pipeline, the government said.</p>
<p>The pipeline was officially opened on Friday by the energy ministers of Algeria, Morocco, Spain and Portugal.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
